==============================================================================
GAP THEOREM (computational, n<=8 exhaustive; edge achieved all n)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 For n-1 distinct gcd-1 integer speeds, the LRC max-collar M(S) is either
     M(S) = 1/n   (the AP-tight family -- the conjectured extremisers)
 or  M(S) >= 2/(2n-1),  with equality at A_n = {1,..,n-2, 2(n-1)}.
 There is NO config with max-collar strictly between 1/n and 2/(2n-1).

 MEANING: LRC's difficulty at each n is concentrated entirely in the AP
 tight family. Every other configuration clears the 1/n floor by a definite
 surplus >= margin(n) = 1/(n(2n-1)) ~ 1/(2n^2). The closest competitor is
 the AP with its apex DOUBLED (S546): doubling the top runner is the minimal
 move off the extremiser, and it lands exactly on the gap edge. So the
 'doubling = pairing' apex (S546/S547/S549) is literally the second-loneliest
 structure -- the boundary of the LRC extremal basin.
